@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmt:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/traditions/> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — coverage of the traditions already carried
#
# The registry is only readable if every tradition stands on the same scale.
# A registered tradition says pm:corpusNamed; without a counterpart on the
# established ones, an absent coverage state would be the commonest value in
# the graph and would mean nothing.
#
# These statements are here rather than in each tradition's own file for one
# reason: the coverage of the whole holding was assessed in one pass on one
# day, and splitting the assessment across twenty-one files would have hidden
# that it was a single act. They belong in the home files as soon as either
# value changes for an individual tradition, and the value that changes is
# the one to move.
#
# The contact routes below are read off the receptions the files already
# record, not off new research. Where a file states its own position, that
# position is used. Where nothing has been decided, it says so.
#

pmt:Upanisadic pm:coverageState pm:placesEntered ; pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented .
pmt:AdvaitaVedanta pm:coverageState pm:placesEntered ; pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented .
